     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Aakash Chopra Analyzes Gurnoor Brar's Success Against New Zealand</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Former India opener Aakash Chopra attributes pacer Gurnoor Brar's effectiveness against New Zealand to his height, high-arm action, and ability to extract steep, awkward bounce from short-of-good-length deliveries. Brar recently recorded career-best figures of 4/30 in the second ODI, dismissing key batters like Tom Latham and Glenn Phillips to help India secure a narrow victory.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/aakash-chopra-analyzes-gurnoor-brars-success-against-new-zea.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The win, decided by the Duckworth-Lewis-Stern method after rain interrupted play, gave India a 2-0 lead in the five-match series. Despite the visitors struggling at 113/7 during their chase, Brar’s performance and contributions from bowlers Auqib Nabi and Anshul Kamboj proved decisive in restricting New Zealand to 134.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the technical analysis and match outcome using the provided source material.</p>
