       <h1>Anti-drug committee member shot in Punjab</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Amandeep Singh, a 27-year-old member of a Kaleke village anti-drug committee, was shot in the thigh at his residence on November 7, 2026. Police report the victim is in stable condition and have identified four local suspects in connection with the attack.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/anti-drug-committee-member-shot-in-punjab.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Authorities are investigating the motive, noting that Singh had previously provided information leading to FIRs against drug peddlers. This incident follows the recent murder of anti-drug activist Parvinder Singh Jhota in October. The shooting occurs as drug-related issues emerge as a significant social and political concern ahead of the 2027 Punjab Assembly elections.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting that incorporates all key details from the source text while maintaining a professional tone.</p>
