     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-08 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Crictracker, ESPN Cricinfo">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Babar Azam Clarifies Role in Pakistan Test Squad Selection</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Ahead of the first Test against Sri Lanka on November 9 in Rawalpindi, Pakistan captain Babar Azam clarified that squad selection remains the responsibility of coaches and selectors. Babar emphasized that his role is to maximize the performance of the players provided to him, rather than dictating the composition of the team.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/babar-azam-clarifies-role-in-pakistan-test-squad-selection.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The squad recently underwent significant restructuring, including the removal of two players and the inclusion of three debutants. Pakistan is currently focused on developing young talent for the next World Test Championship cycle after struggling during their recent tour of England.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the essence of Babar Azam's clarification on his selection role and the context of the upcoming Test series.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source · also covered by 1 more</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/selection-not-in-my-hands-i-simply-give-my-inputs-says-babar-azam-9303/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1561918.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>This brief was written from the original report. The same event was independently covered by the other outlets listed here.</p>
    </div>
       
