       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-08 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Crictracker, ESPN Cricinfo">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Bancroft Focuses on Cricket Amid New Ball-Tampering Claims</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Cameron Bancroft scored 32 runs for Western Australia against England as Usman Khawaja's forthcoming autobiography reignites controversy regarding the 2018 ball-tampering scandal. Khawaja’s book alleges that the plan to use sandpaper was discussed among multiple squad members, contradicting the initial findings of Cricket Australia’s investigation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/bancroft-focuses-on-cricket-amid-new-ball-tampering-claims.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Western Australia coach Beau Casson stated that Bancroft is keen to move on from the past and focus on his professional performance. While Bancroft has not played international cricket since 2019, he remains a prolific scorer for his state. Previous allegations in 2021 regarding bowler involvement were denied by Pat Cummins, Mitchell Starc, Josh Hazlewood, and Nathan Lyon.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the event and the context provided by the source, maintaining proper attribution.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source · also covered by 1 more</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/cameron-bancroft-keen-to-move-on-as-khawajas-book-reignites-ball-tampering-claims-8671/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1561834.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>This brief was written from the original report. The same event was independently covered by the other outlets listed here.</p>
    </div>
       
