       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>BJP Leaders Celebrate LK Advani's 99th Birthday</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>BJP leaders, including party president Nitin Nabin, held a havan and puja at the party headquarters in New Delhi to mark veteran leader Lal Krishna Advani's 99th birthday. The event commemorated the Bharat Ratna awardee’s contributions to the organization and his public life, featuring a video retrospective of his career.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/bjp-leaders-celebrate-lk-advanis-99th-birthday.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Prime Minister Narendra Modi paid tribute to Advani, highlighting his journey from Sindh to his pivotal roles in building the BJP and serving as Deputy Prime Minister. Advani, born November 8, 1927, has now entered the 100th year of his life. Senior party members attended the celebration, which coincided with Diwali.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and captures all key details including the specific event and the politician's age milestone.</p>
