     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Celina Jaitly Shares Emotional Diwali Message Amid Custody Battle</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actor Celina Jaitly marked her second Diwali separated from her sons, Winston, Viraaj, and Arthur, who currently reside in Austria with their father, Peter Haag. In an emotional Instagram post, Jaitly addressed her children, assuring them that she has not abandoned them and remains hopeful for their future despite the ongoing divorce and custody proceedings.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/celina-jaitly-shares-emotional-diwali-message-amid-custody-b.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Professionally, Jaitly is set to return to Hindi cinema after a six-year hiatus. She will star in 'Sister Nivedita', a film directed by Ram Kamal Mukherjee that chronicles the life of Swami Vivekananda’s disciple, Margaret Noble.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a concise and accurate summary of the actor's personal situation and upcoming professional project.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/it-breaks-my-heart-celina-jaitly-shares-emotional-diwali-post-for-sons-living-in-austria/articleshow/135662509.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
