     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Displaced Kashmiri Pandits Demand Comprehensive Rehabilitation Policy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Displaced Kashmiri Pandits are calling on the government for a comprehensive rehabilitation policy and a return to their homeland after 37 years in exile. Activists in the Jagti township argue that current government initiatives, including the PM package of 6,000 jobs and 6,000 flats, are insufficient to address the community's widespread unemployment and poor living conditions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/displaced-kashmiri-pandits-demand-comprehensive-rehabilitati.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Community leaders are demanding a separate homeland with territorial status, citing the difficulty of returning to old homes. Until a permanent solution is implemented, residents are requesting better facilities in camps and increased relief packages to address the ongoing misery and economic challenges faced by the displaced community.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the community's demands and the dissatisfaction with the existing PM package effectively within the word count.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/govt-should-take-concrete-steps-for-our-return-what-displaced-kashmiri-pandits-want-on-diwali-ws-l-10417754.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
