     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Judi Dench Recalls Vin Diesel’s Elaborate Pitch for 'The Chronicles of Riddick'</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>In her new memoir, &quot;Is It Too Late to Make a Run for It?,&quot; actress Judi Dench reveals that Vin Diesel successfully persuaded her to join the cast of &quot;The Chronicles of Riddick&quot; with an extravagant gesture. Diesel visited Dench at the Haymarket Theatre to pitch the role.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/judi-dench-recalls-vin-diesels-elaborate-pitch-for-the-chron.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To seal the deal, Diesel sent Dench a bouquet of flowers described as the &quot;length of a kayak.&quot; Dench admits that she is &quot;far too easily wooed&quot; by such grand floral gestures, which ultimately led her to accept the part in the film.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately synthesizes the anecdote from Dench's memoir and maintains the requested tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/film/news/judi-dench-reveals-she-was-wooed-1236942417/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
