       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Muhurat Trading: Sensex Gains 82 Points, Nifty Hits 25,024</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Business</span> <span>#Markets</span> <span>#Muhurat Trading</span></div>
       <p>Indian benchmark indices concluded Muhurat Trading with gains during the closing auction session, according to Business Standard. The Sensex recorded an increase of 82 points.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/muhurat-trading-sensex-gains-82-points-nifty-hits-25024.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Nifty 50 index also saw positive movement, closing at 25,024 points. This special trading session marks the start of the Hindu accounting year, Samvat.</p><p>Broader markets reflected this positive trend. The Nifty MidCap 100 advanced by 0.77 per cent, while the Nifty SmallCap 100 climbed 0.92 per cent, as reported by Business Standard.</p><p>What to watch: Investor sentiment in upcoming regular trading sessions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and accurately reflects all the provided source material.</p>
