     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-08 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pakistan Clinches Three-Wicket Win Over India in U19 Asia Cup, Rajput's Century in Vain</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#U19 Asia Cup</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Pakistan</span></div>
       <p>Pakistan secured a three-wicket victory over India in their ACC Men's U19 Asia Cup 2026 Group A encounter at Al Amerat on Sunday, November 8. Chasing a target of 209, Pakistan successfully reached the total despite a valiant century from India's top-order batter, Arjun Rajput. This defeat marks India's first loss in the tournament, following their opening Group A win against Nepal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/pakistan-clinches-three-wicket-win-over-india-in-u19-asia-cu.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Arjun Rajput delivered a spectacular performance for India, scoring 107 runs off just 85 balls, an innings punctuated by 11 boundaries and 5 sixes. However, his efforts proved insufficient as India was bowled out for 208 in 46.3 overs. India's top order struggled significantly, with skipper Lakshya Raichandani, Aaryavir Sehwag (22), VK Vineeth, and Yashbardhan Chauhan collectively contributing only 42 runs. Rajput formed key partnerships, including a 44-run stand with wicketkeeper Anvay Dravid and a 64-run stand with Manal Chauhan, who scored 10, to stabilize the innings. Rajput's dismissal in the 36th over, with the score at 170 for seven, triggered a collapse. India then lost Yashveer Goud and Mohit Ulva, reaching 195 for nine before Kavya Prasad Patel added 23 and Ishan Sood remained unbeaten on 2 to push the total to 208.</p><p>Pakistan's chase was anchored by a composed century from middle-order batter Hamza Zaroor, who batted at number seven to score 100 runs off 108 balls, guiding his side home. The defending champions, captained by Farhan Yousaf, showcased a disciplined bowling performance to restrict India. Ali Raza, Rizwanullah, and Niqab Shafiq were the main wicket-takers, each claiming three wickets for 37, 24, and 42 runs respectively. Left-arm bowler Mohammad Sayam also chipped in with one wicket for 27 runs, completing a comprehensive bowling effort.</p><p>This result holds significant implications for India's campaign in Group A, which includes India, Pakistan, Nepal, and UAE. Having defeated Nepal in their initial fixture, this loss to Pakistan means India will need to secure victories in their remaining group games to ensure a strong position in the standings. India is scheduled to face the United Arab Emirates next. Notably, Pakistan has now defeated India in consecutive editions of the U19 Asia Cup, having previously triumphed by 191 runs in the 2025 final. The rivalry continues to deliver intense contests, with Pakistan reaffirming their dominance in this age-group tournament.</p><p>What to watch: India's performance in their upcoming match against the United Arab Emirates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Excellent coverage of the match details and context, including specific player statistics and tournament implications.</p>
