       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>P.T. Usha Files Complaint Over IOA Election WhatsApp Campaign</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Indian Olympic Association president P.T. Usha has lodged a formal complaint with the electoral officer alleging former archer Dola Banerjee violated the Model Code of Conduct. Usha claims a WhatsApp message circulated in Banerjee’s name improperly solicited votes for the 'New Bharat Panel' ahead of the November 9, 2026, Sportspersons of Outstanding Merit elections.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/pt-usha-files-complaint-over-ioa-election-whatsapp-campaign.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Citing clauses regarding fair campaigning and the prohibition of social media publicity, Usha has requested an urgent investigation and appropriate action to ensure a level playing field. She submitted a screenshot of the message as evidence, seeking a resolution before polling commences at 9 a.m. on election day.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the complaint filed by P.T. Usha regarding the alleged Model Code of Conduct violation.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
