     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana Box Office Trends Show Maharashtra Revenue Lead Over Karnataka</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Ramayana – Part I has earned approximately Rs. 176 crores nett in its first three days, with Maharashtra emerging as the highest-grossing market at Rs. 32.96 crores. Despite generating less revenue than Maharashtra, Karnataka leads in total footfall with 7.95 lakh tickets sold compared to Maharashtra's 7.47 lakh, earning Rs. 30.29 crores.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/ramayana-box-office-trends-show-maharashtra-revenue-lead-ove.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Together, these two states account for 36% of the national total. The National Capital Region follows in third place with Rs. 17.95 crores, while Telangana surpassed Gujarat in revenue, despite significant variations in ticket volumes between the two regions. Maharashtra showed strong weekend momentum, witnessing a 67.05% revenue increase on Saturday.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief synthesizes the box office data and the contrast between ticket volume and revenue across regions accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-box-office-maharashtra-beats-yashs-karnataka-in-collections-despite-selling-fewer-tickets-top-10-states-reveal-surprising-trends/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
