     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana – Part I Sees Massive Rs. 45.53 Crore Advance Booking for Day 5</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Ramayana</span> <span>#Advance Booking</span> <span>#Film Industry</span></div>
       <p>The mythological epic &quot;Ramayana – Part I,&quot; featuring Ranbir Kapoor and Yash, is experiencing an extraordinary surge in advance ticket sales for its fifth day, Monday, November 9. As of 8:30 PM on Sunday, November 8, the film had already registered a staggering Rs. 45.53 crores nett in advance bookings across all languages. This impressive figure accounts for 13,15,667 tickets sold across 22,522 shows, indicating immense audience anticipation and setting the stage for what could become the film's biggest single day at the Indian box office.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/ramayana-part-i-sees-massive-rs-4553-crore-advance-booking-f.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The momentum for &quot;Ramayana – Part I&quot; has been building rapidly. Just a day prior, as of 4:30 PM on Saturday, November 7, advance bookings stood at Rs. 19.11 crores, with 4,92,928 tickets sold across 16,559 shows. By a subsequent update, these sales had climbed significantly to Rs. 37.91 crores nett, reflecting approximately 10.68 lakh tickets sold, highlighting a consistent upward trend in audience interest.</p><p>The latest tally of Rs. 45.53 crores represents a substantial growth of an additional Rs. 7.62 crores, marking a 20.10% increase over the immediately preceding update. When compared to Saturday evening’s Rs. 19.11 crore figure, the advance bookings have surged by a remarkable 138.25%, translating to an additional Rs. 26.42 crores in sales within a span of just over 24 hours. Concurrently, ticket sales have witnessed phenomenal growth, escalating from 4.93 lakh to more than 13.15 lakh, an addition of approximately 8.23 lakh tickets since Saturday’s update.</p><p>Geographically, key regions are driving these robust advance bookings. Maharashtra, Karnataka, and the National Capital Region (NCR) have emerged as the three leading markets for Monday’s anticipated collections. At the city level, Bengaluru is at the forefront, followed closely by Mumbai and Delhi, demonstrating widespread excitement for the film across major urban centers.</p><p>What to watch: How &quot;Ramayana – Part I&quot; performs on its fifth day at the box office.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is thorough, accurately processes the provided statistics, and maintains the context of the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-day-5-advance-booking-rs-19-crores-to-rs-45-crores-in-just-over-24-hours-monday-set-to-be-the-films-biggest-day/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
