     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Revanth Reddy Celebrates Deepavali with Indiramma Housing Beneficiaries</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Chief Minister A. Revanth Reddy celebrated Deepavali with a beneficiary family in Parsapur, Kodangal, to promote the state’s Indiramma housing program. He inaugurated the new home of Goripalli Sumitra and Srinivas, sharing a traditional meal with them while urging other Ministers and MLAs to spend the festival with program recipients in their respective constituencies.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/revanth-reddy-celebrates-deepavali-with-indiramma-housing-be.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Indiramma scheme is a flagship government initiative that has completed approximately 2.21 lakh houses across the state. The government has sanctioned 4.5 lakh houses in the first phase and 2.5 lakh in the second, committing roughly ₹40,000 crore to the project and urban housing plans.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive and accurate summary of both the festival initiative and the broader housing scheme statistics.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/revanth-celebrates-deepavali-with-indiramma-house-beneficiary/article71681093.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
