       <h1>Santiago Film Festival Ceremonies Canceled Following Death of Sebastián Lelio</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Santiago Film Festival (Sanfic) canceled its red carpet ceremonies for both the industry and festival sections scheduled for November 6 and 7. The decision followed the unexpected death on November 6 of Chilean director Sebastián Lelio, known for his Oscar-winning film 'A Fantastic Woman.'</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/santiago-film-festival-ceremonies-canceled-following-death-o.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Lelio's passing cast a solemn atmosphere over the festival's closing events, which wrap on November 8. Despite the cancellation of the red carpet, the festival proceeded to announce its prize winners, including the films 'Monguen' and 'Narciso.'</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and brief reporting of the festival's response to the director's death.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
