       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Crictracker, ESPN Cricinfo">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Usman Khawaja defends ball-tampering claims in new book</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Usman Khawaja has defended revelations in his upcoming autobiography, 'Sabr', regarding the 2018 Cape Town ball-tampering scandal. Khawaja asserts that David Warner, Steve Smith, and Cameron Bancroft unfairly bore the blame for the entire Australian squad, stating that knowledge of the incident extended to others in the team.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-08/usman-khawaja-defends-ball-tampering-claims-in-new-book.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Khawaja explained he waited to speak out because he did not want to disrupt the squad while he was still an active player. He maintains that the three sanctioned players were victims of public humiliation and deserve justice, confirming he made a promise to his friend Warner to tell the truth.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a dense, accurate summary of the source material, capturing the essence of the controversy and Khawaja's motivations without fluff.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source · also covered by 1 more</b>
